# What the Equipment grants lasts only while it is attached (CR 613.1f, 301.5c): Bot1's Hero is a Wizard that grows on a
# noncreature spell, as the existing scenarios show. Bot2's Disenchant destroys the Planisphere on turn 4, the Hero is just a Hero
# and a 1/1 again, and the noncreature spell Bot1 casts afterwards (Mox Ruby) puts no counter on it. The Hero token itself stays.

[Bot1 Deck]
Island
Island
Astrologian's Planisphere
Mox Ruby
Island x3
Island x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Plains
Plains
Disenchant
Plains x4
Plains x10

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Plains.Play
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Island#2.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Astrologian's Planisphere.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main2]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Hero Token.Subtypes = Hero; Wizard
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Plains#2.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Disenchant.Cast(Astrologian's Planisphere)
Bot2.Pass
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T5 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Hero Token.Subtypes = Hero
Bot1.Battlefield.Hero Token.Power = 1
Bot1.Battlefield.Hero Token.Counters.PlusOnePlusOne = (absent)
Bot1.Graveyard = Astrologian's Planisphere
